    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41269" root="هلب" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهُ أُهْلُوبٌ</span></b>  <i>He</i> [a horse] <i>has ardour,</i> or <i>impetuosity, in his running &amp;c.:</i> formed by transposition from, or a dial. form of, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُلْهُوبٌ</span>. (M.)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَدْوُهُ ذُو أَهَالِيبَ</span> [<i>His</i> (a horse's) <i>running is of
ardent,</i> or <i>impetuous, modes,</i> or <i>manners</i>]. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَهْلُوبٌ</span> <i>A kind,</i> or <i>way</i> [or speech]: syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَنٌّ</span>
(K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْلُوبٌ</span>: (AO:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَهَالِيبُ</span>. (AO, K.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اهلوبٌ من الثَّنَاءِ</span> <i>A kind,</i> or <i>way, of praising,</i>
or <i>eulogizing.</i> (TA.)

